A marker with no `latest_migration` records watermark -1, which is behind whatever the plugin ships,
so `booping render` prints the remedy notice in place of the render — and still exits 0, because the
caller is a skill-load shell whose only channel is stdout.

The shipped id is wildcarded: the case depends on at least one migration shipping, never on how many.
The template is a real one under cwd, named absolutely because a relative path would resolve against
the plugin root, so a gate regression renders its body and fails on stdout.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
-- fixtures/cwd/probe.md.j2 --
rendered body
-- cmd --
booping render /proc/self/cwd/probe.md.j2
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
**STOP — tell the user:** this project is behind on booping migrations (recorded id -1, latest shipped [..]). Run `/playbook migrate` to bring the vault current, then retry.
-- stderr --
